<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enabling Act of 1933</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Enabling Act of 1933 was a law passed by the German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> on 23 March 1933 that allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a>'s government to issue laws without parliament's approval, even ones departing from the constitution. Passed under intimidation after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag-fire-decree">Reichstag Fire Decree</a>, it gave the Nazis dictatorial powers and ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a>'s parliamentary rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enabling-act-of-1933.jpg" alt="Enabling Act of 1933" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Pahl · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-14439,_Rede_Adolf_Hitlers_zum_Erm%C3%A4chtigungsgesetz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
